<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43038" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scŏpas</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκόπας.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A famous Grecian sculptor of Paros</i>, <i>who flourished between the</i> 97<i>th
				and</i> 105<i>th Olympiads</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8,
				19, § 49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Div.
				1, 13, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4, 8, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 4,
				39, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A very rich Thessalian in the time of
			Simonides</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 86, 352</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 11,
				2, 14</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 4, 24</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
